\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:00\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Layout detection or Document Layout Analysis is\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:02\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 the first step toward fixing that problem.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:05\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Rather than treating a document as a corpus of raw text,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:09\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 layout detection identifies meaningful regions on the page\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:13\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 and figures out where they are and what they represent.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:16\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 It distinguishes between paragraphs, tables, figures, headers, footers, and\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:21\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 captions. In other words, we're no longer just extracting content,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:25\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 we're understanding the structure of the document.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:28\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 This turns out to be incredibly important.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:30\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Preserving layout prevents different sections of text\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:33\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 from getting mixed together and convoluted.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:35\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 It preserves the narrative flow in multi-column documents.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:39\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 It allows you to target specific parts of a page\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:42\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 like totals in a table or key fields in a form.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:45\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 The core idea here is simple but powerful.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:49\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 layout is important. Once you throw it away,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:51\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 understanding becomes fragile and error prone.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:55\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 If you look at real world documents, such\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 2:57\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 as the ones you've seen in the previous lab,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:00\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 they're rarely just blocks of text.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:02\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 They include columns, tables, charts, images,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:05\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 captions, headers, footers, stamps, and annotations.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:10\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 When you explicitly detect and label these components,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:13\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 downstream models know what kind of information they're looking at\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:16\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 before they try to reason over them.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:18\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Once we know what's on the page and where it is,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:21\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 the next question is how should it be read.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:24\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Layout tells us where things are.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:26\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Reading order tells us in what\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:28\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 sequence a human would actually read them.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:31\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 This matters enormously in multi-column layouts or documents\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:35\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 with floating figures and captions.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:38\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Without a reliable reading order,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:40\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 even a clean layout still leaves room for ambiguity.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:43\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Historically, reading order was handled with rules.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:47\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 You would sort regions top to bottom, left to right,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:50\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 maybe apply an X-Y cut algorithm and hope for the best.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:53\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 This works for very clean documents,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:55\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 but breaks down immediately for anything real and complex.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 3:59\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Any columns, sidebars, or floating elements,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 4:02\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 and those heuristics start producing nonsense.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 4:05\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 That changed with LayoutReader.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 4:07\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Instead of rules, it's a learned model trained on ReadingBank dataset\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 4:11\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 over 500,000 annotated pages with correct reading sequences.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 4:15\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Each word gets represented as a tuple\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 4:18\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 containing the word itself and its apparent index.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb6 \strokec7 4:21\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 \strokec2 Along with layout features, word color,\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
